{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027217-manipulation-of-avatars","id":1027217,"title":"Manipulation of Avatars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-05T12:27:01-08:00","id":1027217,"title":"Manipulation of Avatars?","content":"So spirit 5 allows the manipulation of Avatars a la the Gilgul rite.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible for a suitably evil mage to run around stealing Avatars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:02:17-08:00","id":1027233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027217-manipulation-of-avatars#post1027217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So spirit 5 allows the manipulation of Avatars a la the Gilgul rite.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible for a suitably evil mage to run around stealing Avatars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gilgul is a pretty epic feat of vulgar magic, I'd say requiring about 10 successes per Arete plus 5 per Avatar rating of the victim would be a good estimate. It would also require a great deal of time and quintessence, and a fair few contributters, to pull off, and that's if the mage isn't fighting back. I imagine the Gilgul rite is almost never performed solo simply because you'd need a number of mages to keep the victim down long enough while the casters perform the rite without the whole thing botching around them.<br /> So suitably evil, yes, but running around? Probably not.<br /> <br /> Also, it's been reported that anyone who performs the rite will have trouble with their own avatar if they are aware of what their Mage is doing, and I can't imagine any avatar would approve aiding in this. Even an inverted avatar would prefer another mage's became inverted rather than destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-06-2017, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T17:00:47-08:00","id":1027350,"title":"","content":"Lester Giles from <i>Book of Chantries</i> is an Arete 6 Son of the Ether hanging out with the Nephandi. &quot;<i>He has also become interested in developing a means of altering Avatars. He believes he will one day develop a means of converting one Essence into another. He thinks it may even be possible to develop new Avatars.</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T19:43:25-08:00","id":1027382,"title":"","content":"book of chantries is a pretty early book though. still connected to ars magica!<br /> <br /> anyway it takes archmastery of spirit to do really complicated things to avatars(explained in masters of the arts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T04:35:09-08:00","id":1027537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027217-manipulation-of-avatars#post1027217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So spirit 5 allows the manipulation of Avatars a la the Gilgul rite.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible for a suitably evil mage to run around stealing Avatars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I view this much like I view the difference between a lobotomy and a successful brain transplant. The latter is a miraculous feat of surgery that requires overcoming major technological and logistical hurdles. The former can be done with an icepick without even opening the skull. <br /> <br /> If it takes Mastery to perform Gilgul, I think it's Archmastery to more carefully steal and control an Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:24:01-08:00","id":1027586,"title":"","content":"Just a thought. Depending on how you interput it and how far you want to go with it, The Book of Madness Rev. mentions that Nephandus are able to violate the normally protected quintessence that resides in a Mage's Avatar. Now this isn't stealing avatars but but ripping away the quintessence that is the core of the Avatar might have other detrimental effects to the Mage. Possibly even, at least temporarily, weaking the Avatar making magick use by the Mage more difficult, if not nearly impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:51:58-08:00","id":1027653,"title":"","content":"I also think that Archmastery should be needed for this level of manipulation. IF you use Archspheres, of ourse, this means Archspheres, But they're an optional rule. Otherwise, it will need several Spheres (Prime it's a good choice for a start, since Avatars are supposed to be &quot;shards of Prime&quot;). Anycase, this should be an epic fear, requiring a LOT of knolowedge about Avatars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T15:33:07-08:00","id":1028293,"title":"","content":"Personally, I go with the idea for my setting(s) to treat true Avatar manipulation (vis-a-vis destruction, transplanting from extant incarnation to another, et al) as being under the purview (as proposed by some writers) of Spirit:5, Prime:5, as these &quot;spirits&quot; aren't spirits in the more common use of the term: they are the shards/aspects of the essence that exists above/beyond Reality(tm) as we mortals (and even most mages) understand. That is, they are the &quot;god-seed&quot; from the (pre)dawn creation of time/the universe, itself, and from a level quite above most (not all, but most) essences identified as &quot;spirit&quot;. (It also goes well in-hand, for example, with how Mummies -- whose Avatars are incorporated-and-reworked into their mystical identities even more so than mages' are, per the Spell of Life -- require Spirit:5, Prime:5 to be destroyed (including their Sahus/god-selves, which is what the Avatar is identified as in Mummy). That's not an ironclad example, by any means, but it plays again into the &quot;waaaaaayyyyy deeper into the metaphysical pool than DnD&quot; that most of the metaphysics of WoD has been about since Day One... )<br /> <br /> But that's my personal take on it based on applied &quot;real world&quot; metaphysical comparisons coupled with the cross-comparison of things across WoD. Use and abuse as you see fit....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T15:46:01-08:00","id":1028300,"title":"","content":"Yes it makes most sense for it to be Prime in addition to Spirit. Mind and Entropy also feel like possible Spheres for working with an Avatar; maybe it would depend on Mage's Paradigm, and perhaps Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T16:07:49-08:00","id":1028319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027217-manipulation-of-avatars?p=1028300#post1028300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it makes most sense for it to be Prime in addition to Spirit. Mind and Entropy also feel like possible Spheres for working with an Avatar; maybe it would depend on Mage's Paradigm, and perhaps Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly paradigm would play a big role in this, and certain paradigms would probably have Avatar manipulation on this scale an impossibility. The Celestial Chorus, for example, probably wouldn't think it possible that a mage could control an aspect of The One without attaining a level of godhood themselves, so it would be high level archmastery of nothing for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T16:45:39-08:00","id":1028331,"title":"","content":"A couple of editions ago the <i>Technomancer's Toolbox</i> had a Son of Ether <i>barrabbi</i> talisman that stole pieces of people's souls with a Life 3 Mind 4 Spirit 5 effect. It pointed out that catastrophic consequences could result if it were used on someone with an awakened avatar, and the mage responsible was being driven more and more insane from co-opting small pieces of sleeper's souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:44:56-08:00","id":1028966,"title":"","content":"I once had an idea for an NPC that sort of Diablerized mages (a la VtM) and sucked down their Avatar to add to their own Arete and Avatar rating. The rote was provided to him by infernal means (Demon/Outer Being/Maejlin Incarna/other) and was something like Spirit, Mind and Prime at 5 and Entropy at 4 (might have been 5 as well).<br /> <br /> Spirit and Prime to do the actual stealing, Mind to process and integrate the victims experiences and understanding of it's Avatar/Arete into their own self and Paradigm and Prime/Entropy to purge/convert any resonance of the victims Pattern to their own Pattern. He was also capable of stealing Essence/Gnosis/Faith from Spirits (including the Demons he served) and use it as his own power.<br /> <br /> A lesser rote was available as well where the Mage only got a fraction of the power but the Demon did most of the work.<br /> <br /> In any case, I never got around to incorporate the being into my game, but I guess he wouldn't have survived long due to all the Paradox and/or PCs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:21:56-08:00","id":1030721,"title":"","content":"You can steal it, but it doesn't have to do anything you say. I can steal a tiger with a length of rope and a key to its cage, but that doesn't mean it's an idea that will work out great for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}